# Remote denial-of-service issues in the Go standard library and golang.org/x/net inside the upstream
# caddy:2 image (v2.11.7, built on Go 1.26.8 / x/net 0.59.0; fixed in Go 1.26.9 / x/net 0.60.0).
# Caddy only runs when TLS_DOMAIN is set; plain HTTP mode does not start it. No patched caddy image existed on 2026-10-15 or when re-checked on 2026-10-17 (caddy:2 still v2.11.7, same digest). Re-checked 2026-10-22: caddy:2 was rebuilt (new digest) but is still Go 1.26.8 / x/net 0.59.0. Renewed once to 2026-11-14.
# These entries EXPIRE on 2026-11-14, after which the Trivy gate fails again by itself.
# Remove them as soon as the caddy:2 digest in the Dockerfile is bumped to a rebuild on Go >= 1.26.9 and x/net >= 0.60.0.
CVE-2026-78667 exp:2026-11-14
CVE-2026-78669 exp:2026-11-14
CVE-2026-97031 exp:2026-11-14

# Added 2026-10-22: crypto/x509 man-in-the-middle via untrusted intermediate certificates in the Go standard library inside the
# upstream caddy:2 image (still Go 1.26.8 after its 2026-10-21 rebuild; fixed in Go 1.26.10 / 1.27.3). Same exposure as the entries above:
# Caddy only runs when TLS_DOMAIN is set, and plain HTTP mode (including behind a hosting platform's proxy) never starts it.
# Expires with them on 2026-11-14. If caddy:2 has not moved to Go >= 1.26.10 by then, build Caddy with xcaddy on a patched golang image
# instead of renewing again.
CVE-2026-111943 exp:2026-11-14
